.TH FIMAKE 1 "October 2, 2026" "FiMake" "FiMake Manual"
.SH NAME
fimake \- MCP server that lets AI agents read and edit Figma documents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fimake
.RB [ \-\-version | \-V ]
.br
.B fimake
.RB [ \-\-help | \-h | help ]
.br
.B fimake doctor
.br
.B fimake stop
.br
.B fimake install-plugin
.RB [ \-\-dir
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-version-tag
.IR tag ]
.RB [ \-\-no-register ]
.RB [ \-\-yes | \-y ]
.br
.B fimake
.RS
Start the MCP server (transport taken from
.BR TRANSPORT ).
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
The official Figma MCP server is read-only.
.B fimake
lets AI agents work directly in Figma documents \- create, edit,
organize, and read \-
through a local bridge between this server and the Fimake Figma plugin.
.PP
Default setup is
.B one shared server
.RB ( brew\ services\ start\ fimake ,
.B TRANSPORT=streamable-http
) that every MCP client reaches at
.BR http://localhost:10101/mcp .
Only one server can own the port the Figma plugin connects to.
When in doubt, run
.BR "fimake doctor" .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Check the shared server is up and the Figma plugin is registered.
Exit 0 = ready, 1 = action needed.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the shared background server (brew services).
A stdio instance spawned and owned by an MCP client is left alone;
if the port stays held after stopping, point that client at the
shared URL instead.
.TP
.B install-plugin
Download the Figma dev plugin, unzip it, and register it with
Figma Desktop (macOS only).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show help and exit.
.SH INSTALL-PLUGIN FLAGS
.TP
.BR \-\-dir " " \fIpath\fR
Use an existing plugin directory instead of downloading the release zip.
.TP
.BR \-\-version-tag " " \fItag\fR
Download this release tag (default: the running server version).
.TP
.BR \-\-no-register
Only download and unzip; skip Figma settings.json registration.
.TP
.BR \-\-yes ", " \-y
Quit Figma Desktop without asking when it blocks registration.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TRANSPORT=stdio | streamable-http
Default:
.BR stdio .
.B brew services
runs
.BR streamable-http :
one server, clients connect to
.BR /mcp .
.TP
.B PORT
Default:
.BR 10101 .
Serves the MCP endpoint
.B (/mcp)
and the plugin Socket.IO bridge.
.TP
.B TASK_TIMEOUT_MS
Default:
.BR 20000 .
Tool call round-trip budget.
.TP
.B TASK_ACK_TIMEOUT_MS
Default:
.BR 5000 .
Socket ack budget before a send is queued for retry.
.TP
.B CORS_ORIGIN
Default:
.BR * .
Set a real origin for networked use.
.TP
.B JSON_BODY_LIMIT
Default:
.BR 1mb .
Max JSON body on
.BR /mcp .
.TP
.B DEBUG=1
Verbose wire logging.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the shared server in the background:
.PP
.RS
.nf
brew services start fimake
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check the server and plugin are ready:
.PP
.RS
.nf
fimake doctor
.fi
.RE
.PP
Register the Figma plugin (macOS):
.PP
.RS
.nf
fimake install-plugin
.fi
.RE
.PP
Stop the shared server:
.PP
.RS
.nf
fimake stop
.fi
.RE
